+### ToC wipe recovery and heroic admission
+
+After Anub'arak's wipe cleanup, an idle all-bot raid retries the instance script's
+normal entry recovery at most once per 30 seconds. The script keeps control of
+summoning, Tirion ownership and remaining heroic attempts. Existing, engaged or
+defeated bosses are never replaced; zero attempts stay exhausted. Everyone must
+be alive and in the same instance, with no human or unresolved raid slot.
+
+For the initial heroic Barrett click only, the driver receives the matching Call
+of the Crusade prerequisite (3917 for 10 heroic, 3916 for 25 heroic) if missing.
+This is an explicit administrative admission grant to the clicking bot, not an
+earned kill or a raid-wide reward. It persists on that bot; no other achievement,
+attempt count, character, normal raid or human-controlled raid is changed.
+
 Faction-specific events run only for the relevant side, and heroic-only events
 never fire on a normal run. If an event cannot complete (for example, a scripted
 NPC the party let die), the run either stalls for the player or skips the step,
